# wip607: the GLO mixer (GLO 2nd press) has the PERFORM system: FUNC = MUTE mode, FILL = SOLO mode, black keys 1-8 = the tracks, white keys = the next pattern
wait 300
tap GLO
tap GLO
expect view 3
expect curpage 1
expect msmode 0
expect mutes 0
# MUTE mode: black key 3 mutes track 3 (it no longer plays the pad / picks the group), again = unmute; the page stays the same
tapkey b2
expect mutes 1
expect solo 0
expect curpage 1
tapkey b6
expect mutes 2
expect curpage 1
shot glomix_mute.png
tapkey b2
tapkey b6
expect mutes 0
# SOLO mode (FILL tapped): key 5 = solo 5; key 1 added; keys again = off; FILL with solos = all solos off + MUTE mode
tapkey b9
expect msmode 1
tapkey b4
expect solo 5
shot glomix_solo.png
tapkey b0
expect solo 1
tapkey b0
tapkey b4
expect solo 0
tapkey b0
tapkey b9
expect solo 0
expect msmode 0
expect mutes 0
# mute mode again, FUNC with mutes = all unmuted
tapkey b3
expect mutes 1
tapkey b10
expect mutes 0
# a white key = the next pattern (it used to hold a step): stopped = at once
expect pattern 1
tapkey w2
wait 100
expect pattern 3
tapkey w0
wait 100
expect pattern 1
# the mixer's own knobs and SELECT still work
turn SELECT 1
expect curpage 2
